to an outsider the excitement for this  man might come as a bit of a surprise  bong bong Marcus is the son of late  Filipino dictator Ferdinand Marcos who  installed a terror regime in the  Philippines in the 1970s and 80s but at  this campaign rally in the capital  Manila people support bong bong spit for  the vice presidency many want him to  carry on his father's legacy  Marco's will be the one to finish 500  kilometers to the north lies the home  province of the Marcos family Ilocos  Norte is their power base here they've  ruled uncontested for decades holding  every important political office and  here they glorify their troubled past in  the family mausoleum late dictator  Ferdinand Marcos has been lying in state  for more than 20 years there's not a  word about his many victims or the 10  billion US dollars the Marcus's are  believed to have embezzled during his  rule here in Batak City and in fact in  the whole region you'll have a hard time  finding someone who doesn't support the  Marcos family the fact that tens of  thousands of Filipinos were detained  tortured and even killed under the  Marcos rule doesn't seem to make people  here doubt their loyalty in the least  for many here the Marcus's are nothing  but good Samaritans  if we approach them and ask for their  help they always help us out they would  give us cash or other things if we need  to go to the hospital they help us with  paying the bill you think Bongbong  Marcos can't be held accountable for  what his father did he is not involved  your mother died he and his siblings  were still very young when all that  happened what these loyalists seem to  forget  Bongbong Marcos already held high  political positions during the last  years of his father's rule back in  Manila  Maria Lao Enriquez and her companions  are less convinced of Bongbong Marcos  innocence they all fell victim to his  father's regime and now they blame the  son for not taking responsibility he  doesn't like to apologize he said I  won't apologize for the crimes that he  did not commit he said that it was his  father if we really wants to help the  Filipino people they should return the  money that they stole from the coffers  of the bong bong Marcus says he wants to  unify the nation but his current  candidacy and the prospect at yet  another Marcos could at some point be in  charge of the country is polarizing  Filipino society
 

